{number: 63}
{title: Give of Your Best to the Master}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Give of your best to the Master;
Give of the strength of your [G7] youth;
Throw your [C] soul’s fresh, glowing ardor
Into the battle for [G7] truth.
[C] Jesus has set the example,
Dauntless was He, young and [F] brave;
Give [C] Him your loyal devotion;
Give Him the [G7] best that you [C] have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Give of your best to the Master;
Give of the strength of your [G7] youth;
Clad in [C] salvation’s full armor,
Join in the [G7] battle for [C] truth.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Give of your best to the Master;
Give Him first place in your [G7] heart;
Give [C] Him first place in your service,
Consecrate every [G7] part.
Give, [C] and to you will be given;
Held His beloved Son [F] free;
Grate-[C] fully seeking to serve Him,
Give Him the [G7] best that you [C] have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Give of your best to the Master;
Naught else is worthy His [G7] love;
He [C] gave Himself for your ransom,
Giving up glory a-[G7] bove:
Laid [C] down His life without murmur,
You from sin’s ruin to [F] save;
Give [C] Him your heart’s adoration,
Give Him the [G7] best that you [C] have.
{end_of_verse}
